{
  "type": "comfy",
  "name": "MiniMax H3 Image to Video",
  "description": "Image to Video generation with synchronized audio using MiniMax H3, starting from a reference image. Recommended for systems with discrete GPUs and high vRAM.",
  "extendedDescription": "Animate a reference image into a video clip with sound, using MiniMax H3. The image is center-cropped to the chosen resolution and used as the first frame; refer to it as <Picture 1> in the prompt. Describe the action that transpires, camera movement, and what is heard: spoken words in quotes, sound effects, or the type of music. Videos are rendered at 24 frames per second; the Turbo variant uses a distillation LoRA for 8-step generation.",
  "displayPriority": 360,
  "tags": ["MiniMax H3", "audio", "image to video", "high-vram"],
  "backend": "comfyui",
  "category": "create-videos",
  "toolCategory": "edit-images",
  "mediaType": "video",
  "toolInstructions": "Use this workflow to animate an existing image into a short video clip with synchronized audio (image-to-video) using MiniMax H3. The source image becomes the first frame and is center-cropped to the output aspect ratio. Refer to it as <Picture 1> in the prompt and describe the motion, the camera movement and the audio: put any spoken words in quotes and describe sound effects or music. Resource-intensive (high VRAM); only use when the user explicitly asks for a video from an image.",
